cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NIFE, please cite it as below. If you use one of its methods, please also cite the work that introduced it, listed in the references."
title: "NIFE: NIFE Is a Framework for Explanations"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jurandirs/nife"
url: "https://github.com/jurandirs/nife"
abstract: >-
  NIFE is a Python framework for explaining the predictions of machine-learning
  models, organized by kind of explanation, each with its methods and evaluation
  metrics. It provides counterfactual explanations with surrogate decision trees,
  which also show the features that drive a prediction, and metrics to evaluate
  counterfactuals found by any method, for classification and regression.
keywords:
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - counterfactual explanations
  - decision trees
  - interpretability
  - machine learning
